Source: hp-spectre-x360-16
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/BrucePerens/hams_open/tree/main/hardware/hp_spectre_x360_16

Package: hp-spectre-x360-16-support
Architecture: all
Depends: convertible-helper (>= 1.3.0), convertible-power (>= 1.0.0), grub-large-console (>= 1.0.0),
         udev, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: thermald
Description: HP Spectre x360 2-in-1 16-f2xxx hardware support for Debian
 Settings for the HP Spectre x360 2-in-1 Laptop 16-f2xxx on a stock Debian
 GNOME desktop: it pulls in convertible-helper (tablet mode: the on-screen
 keyboard in tablet position, the screen reset to normal when the laptop
 leaves tablet mode) and convertible-power (maximum performance on AC, maximum
 battery life on battery), and adds this laptop's power settings.
 .
 The power settings are applied only when the DMI product name begins with
 "HP Spectre x360 2-in-1 Laptop 16-f".
